{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed56627177/15/prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"4c7dc4dd\" lines=\"7-21\">\n<description>\nLearn a transformation rule from a training pair of framed sprites, then apply it to a test sprite.\n\nInput structure:\n- Grid contains several colored square frames (hollow borders of a single color).\n- Each frame's interior holds a small pattern sprite; one frame's interior is blank (all black).\n- Two frames form a training pair (their interiors share the same color palette); one remaining frame is the test case.\n\nRule:\n- Identify the training pair by matching interior color sets; the other non-blank frame is the test input.\n- Infer the rule mapping source→destination (e.g. reflection, color inversion, gap filling, endpoint extraction, or checkerboard complement).\n- Apply that same rule to the test sprite; output the transformed interior.\n\nKey insight: The puzzle is an analogy — \"A is to B as C is to ?\" — where you must discover the visual rule from one example pair and generalize it.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"984d8a3e\" lines=\"5-21\">\n<description>\nShift each row's dominant middle-color run left until its right edge aligns with the leftmost original right edge, moving displaced left-side pixels after the run.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has three colors.\n- The most common color forms one contiguous horizontal run in every row.\n- Pixels before those runs share one side color, and pixels after those runs share the other side color.\n\nRule:\n- Find the minimum right edge column among the middle-color runs.\n- In each row, keep the run width and the trailing right-side color count.\n- Place the middle-color run so its right edge is at that minimum column, unless the run is too wide, in which case start it at column 0.\n- Fill any remaining non-trailing cells with the left-side color.\n\nKey insight:\nThe varying row prefixes are movable padding; the stable feature is the leftmost right boundary of the middle-color shape.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"78e78cff\" lines=\"71-91\">\n<description>\nRecolor the row-wise passage indicated by wall pixels with the singleton marker color.\n\nInput structure:\n- A dominant background contains one singleton marker pixel and one wall color.\n- Wall pixels lie on several rows and form left/right limits around the marker column.\n- Empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows are open horizontal passages.\n\nRule:\n- On a wall row, paint background pixels between the nearest wall strictly\n  left of the marker column and the nearest wall at or right of it; if only\n  one side is present, paint from that wall to the opposite grid edge.\n- On empty rows between the top and bottom wall rows, paint the whole row.\n- On empty rows outside the wall-row band, reuse the nearest end wall-row interval.\n- Preserve wall pixels and the original marker pixel.\n\nKey insight:\n- The wall color defines scanline limits relative to the marker column; the\n  marker color fills those implied horizontal spans rather than flood-filling\n  through connected background.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2601afb7\" lines=\"30-45\">\n<description>\nRotate each vertical bar's color one slot right and its height one slot left.\n\nInput structure\n- A dominant background surrounds several monochrome one-cell-wide vertical bars.\n- Every bar is bottom-aligned and occupies a distinct column.\n- The ordered bar slots are read from left to right.\n\nRule\n- Keep the grid shape and the bar columns unchanged.\n- At slot i, use the color from the previous slot cyclically.\n- At slot i, use the height from the next slot cyclically.\n\nKey insight\n- Color and height are independent cyclic attributes of the ordered bar slots:\n  colors rotate right while heights rotate left.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"db0c5428\" lines=\"32-51\">\n<description>\nExpand a 3x3 block motif into a 5x5 block motif around its missing center.\n\nInput structure:\n- Teal background surrounds one 9x9 foreground motif.\n- The motif is a 3x3 array of 3x3 blocks; the middle block is empty teal.\n- Colored pixels immediately around the empty middle block encode the border\n  of the missing center block.\n\nRule:\n- Keep the original 9x9 motif in place.\n- Copy each of the eight surrounding 3x3 blocks to the opposite outer slot\n  of the implied 5x5 block grid, without rotating it.\n- Fill the center block from the eight pixels around the hole; its center is\n  the motif's majority foreground color.\n\nKey insight: The visible 9x9 motif is the middle of a larger periodic\nblock-level pattern, and the empty center is reconstructed from its immediate\ninner boundary.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6ca952ad\" lines=\"15-30\">\n<description>\nDrop every large foreground object straight down to the bottom while leaving small marker objects fixed.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid has a dominant background color and exactly one foreground color.\n- The foreground is split into separated 4-connected objects.\n- Objects of area at most three are stationary markers; larger objects are moving sprites.\n\nRule:\n- Clear each moving sprite from its original position.\n- Translate each moving sprite vertically downward until its bbox bottom reaches the grid bottom.\n- Repaint each translated sprite in its original color; small markers stay unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- Object area separates the active falling sprites from the small fixed markers, and all active sprites follow the same vertical path.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"230f2e48\" lines=\"19-38\">\n<description>\nFold each straight red rod at its black marker, leaving the gray-anchored side fixed.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Each foreground object is a straight horizontal or vertical 4-connected rod.\n- Each rod contains many pixels of one line color, one endpoint marker, and one\n  interior control marker.\n\nRule:\n- For every rod, keep the segment from the endpoint marker through the control\n  marker unchanged.\n- Move the line-color tail on the far side of the control marker to a\n  perpendicular ray starting next to that marker.\n- Choose the perpendicular direction with more space to the grid edge.\n\nKey insight:\n- The endpoint marker identifies the fixed side of the rod, while the control\n  marker is the hinge; the tail folds into the larger open half-plane.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3d588dc9\" lines=\"95-109\">\n<description>\nReplace the active black cutout's tail with background and mark the cutout side facing a colored source region.\n\nInput structure:\n- The dominant color is background, with black rectangle-plus-tail cutouts, one gray source region, and colored distractors.\n- Non-gray colored regions and single pixels are distractors/blockers, even when they are multi-pixel staircase shapes.\n\nRule:\n- Find each black cutout whose largest solid rectangle leaves exactly a two-pixel tail.\n- The active gray source region is visible only by horizontal rays through background from a cutout's left or right side.\n- Select the unique cutout side with the most same-source visible rows, erase that cutout's tail to background, and recolor the full selected vertical side pink (6).\n\nKey insight:\n- The colored regions do not move; their horizontal line-of-sight identifies which rectangular cutout is being opened and which side receives the pink mark.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5751f35e\" lines=\"29-43\">\n<description>\nComplete sparse nested rectangular color layers into solid rectangles.\n\nInput structure\nThe background is the dominant color, and every foreground color marks one\naxis-aligned rectangular layer; the layer bboxes have unique areas and are\nnested from outermost to innermost.\nRule\nTake each color's bbox as its completed rectangle, except that a child bbox\nwhich already matches at least three sides of its parent's one-pixel inset\nexpands to that full inset; repaint the rectangles largest to smallest.\nKey insight\nThe scattered pixels are samples of nested rectangular regions, so the\noutput is a clean redraw of those regions with inner colors overwriting\nouter colors.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"41ace6b5\" lines=\"7-26\">\n<description>\nNormalize vertical two-color bars between paired marker columns around the marker rows.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- A row of red marker pixels sits directly above a row of gray marker pixels\n  in the same alternating columns.\n- The columns between adjacent markers contain vertical bars made from a\n  contiguous teal run above a contiguous blue run.\n\nRule\n- Keep the marker pixels and all non-bar background cells fixed.\n- Let h be the maximum teal-run height among the bar columns; paint teal in\n  every bar column for h rows ending at the red marker row.\n- In each bar column, move its blue run to start at the gray marker row and\n  fill all lower cells in that column with maroon.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker rows are a baseline: teal is normalized into a common upper\n  band, while each blue run keeps its own height below the baseline.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e39e9282\" lines=\"73-81\">\n<description>\nProject maroon markers into adjacent grey or pink 3x3 squares, erasing grey squares afterward.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
